Toast POS — Offline-First POS Order Ingestion & Payment Sync Engine
Problem Context
You are designing the architecture for Toast’s handheld Point-of-Sale (POS) terminals. Handheld terminals operate inside busy restaurants where Wi-Fi frequently drops. Servers must be able to take orders and swipe credit cards completely offline, and the system must reconcile state with the cloud once connectivity is restored.
1. Functional Requirements (FRs)
Offline Order Creation & Local Storage: POS terminals must accept orders, add items, apply discounts, and print kitchen tickets locally when network connection is 100% offline.
Offline Payment Processing: Process credit card transactions offline by storing encrypted payment tokens locally and queueing them for cloud gateway authorization upon reconnection.
Idempotent Cloud Sync & Conflict Resolution: When a terminal reconnects, it syncs its local event log to the cloud without creating duplicate orders or double-charging cards.
Concurrent Multi-Terminal State Sync: Multiple servers using different POS handhelds at the same table must observe real-time order updates when online.
2. Scale & Non-Functional Constraints
Scale: 100,000+ active restaurants, 500,000 POS terminals, 50 Million daily transactions.
Offline Budget: Terminal must support running offline for up to 72 hours continuously.
Sync Latency: On network reconnection, batch sync must complete in $< 2$ seconds.
Data Guarantee: At-Most-Once payment authorization (Zero Double Charging).
3. Staff-Level Deep-Dive Focus Areas (What the Interviewer Will Probe)
Local Storage & Write-Ahead Logging (WAL): How do you structure the embedded database (e.g., SQLite / Couchbase Lite) on the Android POS device to guarantee zero data loss if the battery dies mid-order?
Conflict Resolution Strategy: Server A (offline) removes an item from Table 5. Server B (online) adds an item to Table 5. How do you resolve conflicting offline updates when Server A reconnects? (Vector Clocks, CRDTs, or Event Sourcing).
Offline Payment Risk Management: How do you bound financial liability when authorizing credit card transactions offline before contacting the bank gateway?